    },
    {
     "name": "Luis's agent",
     "role": "a real pro's own agent: bid, win, work, get paid (stopped: could never be hired)",
     "via": "A2A",
     "blocker": 0,
     "bug": 0,
     "confusing": 0,
     "report": "round1-luis.md"
    }
   ],
   "outcome": "No money moved wrongly. Every attempt by Rin was refused, and the ledgers stayed balanced: raising prices, injecting amounts, an outside payee, releasing without permission, releasing after a cancel, other people's jobs, and hiring a pro with no verified PayPal. But no customer's job reached payment: demo pros never worked a job a visitor or an agent hired. A pro created by staff could never verify PayPal, so neither Luis nor Rin's pro could be hired, and the evidence-fraud tests did not run. One malformed offer blanked the job page, and the judge tour put a customer into the staff back office.",
   "fixes": [
    "Demo pros now do the jobs they are hired for: BEFORE photos, fresh AFTER photos with EXIF, a receipt, then submit. There is also a demo-only 'Have the demo pro finish now' button.",
    "Pro onboarding: a one-time sign-in link to verify PayPal, licence and insurance. readiness and my_profile tell a pro's agent what blocks hiring, and an offer from a pro who can't be hired yet is flagged.",
    "Demo pros wait about 60 s before bidding and never decline a real pro's offer.",
    "Agents can no longer post a budget above the per-job limit. Pros can't mint customer tokens and can't see competitors' offers.",
    "accept_offer with no saved payment falls back to an approval link, and a failed hold can be retried (retry_hold). The buffer never takes the hold above the budget.",
    "/api/staff/* refuses customer sessions. The tour ends on a labelled, read-only, anonymised back office.",
    "The job page can't be blanked by one bad field (guarded fields, an error boundary per panel). A pending hold is no longer shown as held, rules are shown in plain words, and scope suggestions can be applied before posting.",
    "Moving the demo clock needs a person on the website or demo staff, and the site shows who moved it.",
    "llms.txt lists every tool's arguments, and post_job accepts 'description'."
   ]
  },
