   ],
   "outcome": "For the first time a customer's job went from posting to payout. Jamie paid $195: $175.50 went to the pro and $19.50 was the fee, and the unused $39 of the hold was never charged. Maria's agent reached all checks done in 5 min 13 s, then waited for Maria to confirm the photos, because no vision model was serving. No money moved wrongly. Rin's fake photos all failed: no timestamp, dated 15 days early, taken in New York, reused, or the platform's own demo pictures. So did a receipt with the wrong date and instructions written into notes. But a photo caption carrying instructions was not flagged, and a drain job passed on evidence about a valve. An agent could not set milestone options or hand its person a link for a person-only step, no inspector existed, and a real pro still never won a job.",
   "fixes": [
    "Agents can set job options when posting and change them until an offer is accepted. There is a review_scope tool, and the demo inspector always exists.",
    "Person-only steps (a limit, a ceiling, confirming photos) come with a one-time link the agent shows its person.",
    "The customer's agent can read its own job's evidence. Time-gap conditions are checked against the photos' timestamps.",
    "Each condition is checked against its own wording: a licence number needs a TSBPE-format number, and evidence about a different job doesn't pass. Every text field on a photo is scanned for instructions.",
    "Parts are paid at the receipt amount, not the change order's. A pro can resend evidence while the job is in review, and can withdraw an offer.",
    "Demo pros send evidence that fits the job type, and there is one source of truth for who decided each check.",
    "The pro feed shows every open job in the pro's trade and radius. Pros get wait_for_news and a rates tool, and the onboarding routes are documented.",
    "Website: one wording for who decided, offers that stay in place, the decision first on phones, no raw ids, a bottom-sheet tour, and Payout sent kept apart from Paid."
   ]
  },
