   "outcome": "Maria's agent ran a whole job over MCP for the first time, from post to payout sent, in 22 minutes. Maria approved the hold and confirmed the photos through the links the server gave her agent. She paid $175; $157.50 went to the pro, $17.50 was the fee, and $25 of the hold was never charged. Jamie's job was paid on the website. Luis, a real pro, won a job and finished it. One blocker: money moved wrongly when Rin, as the customer on the website, used confirm on a job whose checks had failed. It captured $187.05 and paid the pro, and it reproduced on a second job. The release route correctly refused the same thing. The red team's other attempts held: fake photos, photos out of order, padded parts, injected captions and offer games. A demo pro's unchanged permit kept Dana's milestone from ever passing, demo customers left change orders unanswered, and demo pros moved the shared clock.",
   "fixes": [
    "confirm refuses when any check failed. One guard in the capture path covers every way money can move: it captures only when every condition passed or a person acknowledged each failed one.",
    "The hold never goes above the ceiling except for approved change orders, and offers above the ceiling are marked as such. post_job accepts milestones.",
    "An undated receipt goes back to the pro unless they type a date inside the window.",
    "Demo pros answer what each fix request asks for. An identical resend is refused, water-heater scenes match the job, and the plate's capacity is checked against the scope.",
    "Demo pros never move the shared clock. Demo customers decide change orders and confirm finished work within minutes.",
    "Every review_scope suggestion can be applied. A licence number already registered to another pro is flagged.",
    "There is one source of truth for the buffer wording, and the batch status no longer hides unclaimed payout items.",
    "Website: the job page refreshes itself, one line explains the payout state, the checks headline counts what waits for a person, there is one main confirm-and-pay button, and a separate release-anyway that names the failed checks."
   ]
  },
