   "outcome": "Four of the five jobs were paid and every ledger balanced. Maria's agent paid $180 over MCP: $137.70 to the pro and $24.30 to the helper, and $20 of the hold was never charged. Luis, a real pro, was paid for the first time: $168.34 of $187.05, with his $47.05 parts change order approved by the demo customer in about 90 s. Jamie paid $185 on the website. Round 4's blocker is closed: confirming over failed checks is refused on every path, and padded parts were captured only at the receipt's $47.05. One blocker remained. On Dana's water heater, the permit check failed the demo pro's permit three times with a reason that contradicted its verdict. Applying scope suggestions also dropped the milestone's permit and inspection conditions.",
   "fixes": [
    "The permit check passes a permit with a number, issue date and site, and every reason matches its verdict. Applying suggestions never drops existing conditions or milestone documents.",
    "BEFORE photos sent with start_work count, and the AFTER-after-BEFORE order rule is enforced. Evidence for a condition accumulates instead of being replaced.",
    "Change orders can be decided while a job is in review. A change order over the agent's limit carries the person's link.",
    "Receipts and documents get the same reuse detection across jobs as photos.",
    "Offers can state parts. A licence missing from the registry goes to staff review, and a pro's wait_for_news shows only their own jobs.",
    "After a scope suggestion is applied, offers are requested again.",
    "The live-test history is served at /live-test and linked from the footer.",
    "Website: a pay confirmation that is the customer's choice, a demo payout-address label, per-photo captions, plain wording for the tour and the Models page, the cancel button set apart, and the demo sign-in described plainly."
   ]
