   "outcome": "Dana's two-milestone water heater ran end to end with the models on. $1,400 was captured: $140 in fees, $1,071 to the pro, $189 held as retainage, and $350 of the buffer released. Jamie's drain job was paid on the website. The PIN held for most person-only actions: an agent without it couldn't raise limits, create tokens, or sign in through a link. Two gaps remained. An agent applied scope suggestions alone, which dropped the permit and inspection conditions. On Dana's job the agent's release went through with agent release turned off. We count that second gap as a blocker even though the tester didn't, because money moved without permission. The vision model misread honest camera photos (\"a cartridge in a printer\"), which sent Luis and Maria into fix loops; retaking one photo also broke a timed condition on another. The judge tour stalled at step 2. One red-team brief was declined by the model as unsafe and was rewritten as a safeguard check.",
   "fixes": [
    "Every money-moving agent path checks the agent's release permission. Applying all suggestions, or any suggestion that loosens the scope, needs the person; no suggestion can drop a condition or a milestone document.",
    "A photo the vision model can't recognise goes to a person, not back to the pro. Only problems code can prove send a photo back.",
    "Plate and label conditions read the plate with OCR first, and an \"area cleared\" condition can't pass on a label close-up.",
    "Retaking a referenced photo marks the conditions timed from it as needing a retake. The pro is warned before submitting, and negative durations are never shown.",
    "The person can confirm conditions one at a time. A pro can ask a person to look, and is told when an offer is withdrawn.",
    "Parts are paid at cost on milestone jobs too. The tour completes in under a minute.",
    "Website: the PIN window is explained and the hire dialog says PayPal is simulated."
   ]
  },
